{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-im-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.83: `rates-im` -- `im-cook` at Rates scale (MESOSCALE_LOOKUP): THC, CO, NOx and NMHC at running and start exhaust for the motorcycle (11), passenger car (21) and single-unit short-haul truck (52), every fuel MOVES adds, Cook County, Illinois (17031), DEFAULT domain, 2020, August, weekday, hour 7, from the default database alone.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the I/M blend on the RATE path: BaseRateCalculator blends emissionRate with emissionRateIM by the same IMAdjustFract as meanBaseRate (baseratecalculator.go:1194), and the rate tables are written from BaseRateOutput, so RatePerDistance, RatePerStart and RatePerVehicle carry the blended rates of the covered cohorts -- 21's at model years 1996-2016 and 52's at 1980-2015, the latter at IMFactor's fractional values -- at every speed bin. StartsPerVehicle carries no rate. 11 has no program.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 4 and `n_physicsRow` 23 from `sampleVehiclePopulation` and `sourceUseTypePhysics` for 11, 21 and 52; `n_ratesScale` 1.\n\nNo `db_movesoutput` here: a Rates run's oracle is its rate tables.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "inspection-maintenance"
    ]
  },
